      "q": "1. Imagine you receive a letter from someone living in the Gupta Empire. The letter starts like this:\n\u201cGreetings from P\u0101\u1e6daliputra! Life here is vibrant and full of excitement. Just yesterday, I witnessed ...\u201d Complete the letter with a short paragraph (250\u2013300 words) describing life in the Gupta Empire.",
      "a": "Greetings from P\u0101\u1e6daliputra! Life here is vibrant and full of excitement. Just yesterday, I witnessed a grand procession of scholars and artists heading to the king\u2019s court. The city\u2019s lanes are kept clean, and prosperous traders from distant lands fill the bazaars with beautiful wares. The great Nalanda University attracts students from all over India and even China. Our king, Chandragupta II Vikram\u0101ditya, rules with justice and encourages learning, arts, and music\u2014the performances at court are always delightful.\nPeople are generous, as heads of Vaishya families have set up houses for charity and medicines; the sick and needy are cared for. Children learn from elders, and temples are abuzz with magnificent sculptures being created. You can find the iron pillar of Delhi standing strong without rust, a tribute to the advanced skills of our craftsmen. Our land is divided into provinces, and efficient governance keeps peace and prosperity.\nSociety is harmonious\u2014Buddhists, Hindus, and others live and learn together, and festivals fill us all with joy. Life in the Gupta Empire feels like a golden age, inspiring pride and hope for the future. Wish you could be here to see it all!"
